<title>UK: NWE straight-run fuel oil weakens again.</title>
<headline>NWE straight-run fuel oil weakens again.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-01-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>NWE low sulphur straight-run fuel oil was weaker again on Wednesday as cracked prices and swaps fell by some $5 per tonne, traders said.</p>
<p>One regular seller assessed fob prices for North Sea cargoes &quot;in the mid 130s&quot; although buyers said this was optimistic.</p>
<p>High sulphur markets held their ground better along with stronger crude and stable cracked prices.</p>
<p>-- London newsroom +44 171 542 8167</p>
